<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 31,017 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 31,017 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 31,017 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday, compared to 26,315 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 9,607	   12,393</p>
<p>    Import cargo			21,410	   13,922</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  56,000	 Thebro		19/1</p>
<p>Naph oil		 11,000	 Trogir		20/1</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	   13,000	 Cielo-Di-Milano    due</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-1	   22/1</p>
<p>High speed diesel    27,300	 Chilham Castle    24/1</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,125	 Harmony Breeze     due</p>
<p>High speed diesel    75,000	 Chesapeak City     due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
